# kernel-frv.img -- Linux 4.9.337 for the MB93091 VDK (Fujitsu FR-V FR401, noMMU)
#
# Runs on qemu-system-frv -M mb93091 from the qemu fork (lordrasmus/qemu,
# branch uclibc-ng); upstream qemu never had FR-V.  The image is the
# stripped vmlinux (ELF).
#
#   qemu-system-frv -M mb93091 -nographic -kernel kernel-frv.img \
#     -drive if=none,id=hd,format=raw,file=rootfs.ext2 \
#     -device virtio-blk-device,drive=hd \
#     -append "console=ttyS0 root=/dev/vda rootfstype=ext2 rw \
#              virtio_mmio.device=0x200@0xfc000000:5"
#
# The disk sits on the virtio-mmio slot the qemu fork adds to the board
# (0xfc000000, external interrupt XIRQ4 = IRQ 5); the real board has none.
# -initrd rootfs.img.xz still works for a rootfs that fits in RAM.
#
# The machine is the mb93090-mb00 motherboard without PCI, with an FR401
# (MB93401A) CPU board: the FR400 core uClinux runs on, which the
# uClibc-ng toolchain's -mcpu=fr400 code needs.  RAM is 256 MiB at
# 0xc0000000.  Linux registers both on-chip UARTs as line 0, so the second
# one (0xfeff9c40) becomes ttyS0; qemu connects serial0 there.  qemu puts
# the command line at the top of RAM and the initrd below it, and appends
# initrd=<start>,<size> to the command line.
#
# 4.9 is the last line with frv (removed in v4.17; 4.9 is the last
# longterm kernel that has it).
#
# Patches, each one fix, against linux-4.9.337:
#   kernel-frv-initrd.patch        take the initrd from initrd=<start>,<size>;
#                                  BLK_DEV_INITRD was off for frv
#   kernel-frv-clock-cmodes.patch  section type conflict with gcc 15
#   kernel-frv-dma-nopci.patch     the DMA operations were only built with PCI
#   kernel-frv-sdata-aw.patch      .sdata of switch_to.S had no flags and was
#                                  not loaded: stack pointer 0 after head.S
#   kernel-frv-uart-mapbase.patch  without a mapbase the 8250 driver never
#                                  configured the UARTs: no output from
#                                  user space
#   kernel-readahead-tmpfs.patch   readahead(2) on tmpfs (shared with tile
#                                  and cris)
#
# Build: kernel-frv.config is allnoconfig with FR401, MB93091_VDK,
# MB93090_MB00 without PCI, UCPAGE_OFFSET_C0000000, GPREL_DATA_NONE,
# BINFMT_ELF_FDPIC, SERIAL_8250(_CONSOLE) with 2 UARTs, BLK_DEV_INITRD with
# RD_XZ, DEVTMPFS(_MOUNT), TMPFS, SYSVIPC, POSIX_MQUEUE, the event fds,
# inotify, NET, INET, UNIX, PACKET, PRINTK_TIME,
# SECTION_MISMATCH_WARN_ONLY, and VIRTIO_MMIO(_CMDLINE_DEVICES), VIRTIO_BLK
# and EXT2_FS for the root disk.
#
#   cd linux-4.9.337
#   for p in kernel-frv-initrd.patch kernel-frv-clock-cmodes.patch \
#            kernel-frv-dma-nopci.patch kernel-frv-sdata-aw.patch \
#            kernel-frv-uart-mapbase.patch kernel-readahead-tmpfs.patch
#   do patch -p1 < $p; done
#   cp kernel-frv.config .config
#   make ARCH=frv CROSS_COMPILE=frv-openadk-linux-uclibc- \
#        HOSTCFLAGS=-fcommon olddefconfig vmlinux
#   frv-openadk-linux-uclibc-strip -o kernel-frv.img vmlinux
#
# The toolchain is the CI's toolchain-frv-gcc-15.3.0-no-shared-nommu-fdpic.
